<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-grăvĭdo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. a. (late Lat.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To make pregnant</i>, <i>impregnate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coëuntes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 24, 352</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To weigh down</i>, <i>burden</i>, <i>oppress.</i>—Part.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingrăvĭ-dātus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>burdened</i>, <i>oppressed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectus curis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 7, 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
